Instagram Hook Generator

Turn a creator's niche and content script into 5 scroll-stopping hooks.

Step 1: Collect inputs

Ask the user these two questions. If they've already given an answer in the conversation, don't ask it again.

What is your Instagram niche? (e.g., fitness for busy moms, personal finance for Gen Z, skincare, travel on a budget, SaaS founder tips)
What is your content script? Ask them to paste the full script or a clear summary of the Reel/post: the main point, the story, and the takeaway.

Ask both in one short message. Don't proceed until you have both. If the script is vague (fewer than ~2 sentences), ask one follow-up for the core point or payoff.

Step 2: Analyze before writing (internally)

Before writing hooks, identify:

The audience in this niche and their biggest pain, desire, or fear
The core promise or payoff of the script
The most surprising, specific, or emotional element in the script (a number, a result, a mistake, a contrarian take)
Step 3: Write 5 hooks

Write exactly 5 hooks, each using a different angle. Use these angles, one each:

Curiosity gap: opens a loop the viewer needs closed ("Nobody tells you this about...")
Bold or contrarian claim: challenges a common belief ("Stop doing X. It's why you're not growing.")
Specific result or number: concrete outcome, timeframe, or stat ("I gained 10k followers in 30 days doing one thing.")
Pain-point callout: speaks directly to a frustration ("If your Reels get stuck at 200 views, watch this.")
Story or pattern interrupt: a mini-story, confession, or unexpected opener ("I almost quit last year. Then I found this.")
Hook quality rules
Short: spoken hooks under ~12 words; on-screen text under ~8 words.
Specific over generic: use details from the user's script. No filler like "Hey guys" or "In today's video".
Honest: the hook must be delivered by the script. No clickbait the content can't pay off.
Natural spoken language: it should sound like a person talking, not an ad.
No clichés: avoid "game-changer", "you won't believe", "secret hack" unless truly earned.
Niche-native: use the vocabulary the niche's audience actually uses.
Step 4: Output format

For each hook provide:

Hook #N: [Angle name]

Spoken line: the exact first line to say
On-screen text: a shorter version for the text overlay
Why it works: one sentence

Then end with:

Top pick: which hook is strongest for this script and why (one sentence)
Offer: ask if they want the 5 hooks rewritten in a different tone (funnier, more serious, more aggressive) or want a matching first-3-seconds visual idea for any hook.
Example

Input

Niche: Personal finance for college students
Script: Explains that most students waste money on subscriptions, shows how to audit them in 5 minutes, and saves $47/month.

Output (abridged) Hook #1: Curiosity gap

Spoken line: "There's a $47 leak in your bank account right now, and you've never noticed it."
On-screen text: "Your hidden $47/month leak"
Why it works: Creates an open loop around something personal and money-related.

(...continue through Hook #5, then Top pick and Offer.)
